{#
  Sent once, on the third consecutive day a reader's edition fails.

  A daily apology through a prolonged outage is worse than silence, so this
  replaces the failure notice and nothing further is sent until an edition is
  actually delivered. It is a system state, not the reader's subscription
  status: their subscription is untouched and delivery resumes on its own.
#}
<table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="background:#f4f2ee;margin:0;padding:0;">
<tr><td align="center" style="padding:20px 10px;">
<table role="presentation" width="560" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="width:560px;max-width:100%;background:#ffffff;">
  <tr><td style="padding:26px 28px 14px 28px;border-bottom:3px double #141414;">
    <h1 style="margin:0;font-family:'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif;font-size:28px;line-height:1.1;color:#141414;">
      {{ brand }}
    </h1>
  </td></tr>
  <tr><td style="padding:22px 28px 26px 28px;">
    <p style="margin:0 0 14px 0;font-family:Georgia, serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:#242424;">
      {{ first_name }},
    </p>
    <p style="margin:0 0 14px 0;font-family:Georgia, serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:#242424;">
      Your edition hasn't arrived for a few days now, and we'd rather tell you
      once than apologise every morning.
    </p>
    <p style="margin:0 0 14px 0;font-family:Georgia, serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:#242424;">
      We've paused these notices while we sort it out. Your subscription is
      unchanged, and your edition will simply start arriving again — you don't
      need to do anything.
    </p>
    <p style="margin:24px 0 0 0;font-family:Georgia, serif;font-size:11px;line-height:1.5;color:#8a8a8a;">
      <a href="{{ preferences_url }}" style="color:#8a8a8a;">Manage your preferences</a>
      &nbsp;·&nbsp;
      <a href="{{ unsubscribe_url }}" style="color:#8a8a8a;">Unsubscribe</a>
    </p>
  </td></tr>
</table>
</td></tr>
</table>
